# apps/web: copy to apps/web/.env.local and fill in. That file is gitignored,
# and this repository is public: never commit a real value.
#
# ⚠️ Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the browser bundle and
# ships to every visitor. Only values that are public by design may carry it.
#
# Tiers: local values go here. Preview and production values live in the
# Vercel project's Environment Variables, one set per environment. See
# "Environments and secrets" in the root AGENTS.md.

# --- Shopify Storefront API (server-only) ---
# Not NEXT_PUBLIC_: every query runs in a Server Component, so the token never
# needs to reach the browser. packages/shopify's smoke test reads this file too.
SHOPIFY_STORE_DOMAIN=your-store.myshopify.com
SHOPIFY_STOREFRONT_TOKEN=
SHOPIFY_API_VERSION=2026-04

# --- Klaviyo onsite (public by design) ---
# The PUBLIC six-character site key, and the LIST (never a segment) that the
# email capture subscribes to. Both are designed to ship in client code: a key
# that can only write events for one account, and a list id that names a
# destination, not a permission. A Klaviyo PRIVATE key must never appear here.
# Leave both empty to render the site without Klaviyo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KLAVIYO_PUBLIC_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_KLAVIYO_LIST_ID=

# --- PostHog product analytics (public, SHO-87) ---
# The project's public API key (starts phc_), EU Cloud. Safe in the bundle,
# like the Klaviyo public key. Nothing is sent before the shopper accepts the
# cookie banner. Leave empty and no analytics run at all.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=

# --- Site URL ---
# The origin canonicals, Open Graph URLs and the sitemap are built from. Not
# secret. Production sets it, on Vercel's Production environment only, to
# https://www.doublehelixsupplements.co.uk. Without it production would fall
# back to the domain Vercel picks for the project, which may be the bare
# domain that only redirects to www. Previews leave it to that fallback and
# point their canonicals at production (see lib/site.ts). Locally, leave empty.
SITE_URL=

# --- App links (optional) ---
# Let product and collection links open the app (lib/app-links.ts). Without
# them /.well-known/apple-app-site-association and assetlinks.json are 404s and
# links open in the browser. Not secret. Production only; redeploy after
# setting. APPLE_TEAM_ID is on Apple Developer > Membership; the Android
# fingerprint (AB:CD:..., comma-separated if several) is in `eas credentials`.
# A Play Store install is signed with Play's key instead, so add the "App
# signing key certificate" SHA-256 from Play Console (Release > Setup > App
# signing) beside the EAS one.
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
ANDROID_CERT_SHA256=
